# Flutter Notifications integration — Cursor prompt

Builds on top of the FCM token registration in [Flutter-fcm.plan](Flutter-fcm.plan). Adds:

1. Receiving admin **broadcast push notifications** (`type: "ADMIN_BROADCAST"`).
2. In-app **Notifications Inbox** screen (history of broadcasts the user can re-read).
3. Optional **Admin "Send Push Notification" screen** inside the Flutter app for users with `role: admin | superadmin`.

Copy everything below the rule into Cursor inside the Flutter repo. Adjust state-management + routing names to match the project before pasting.

---

## Backend contract (locked)

Base: `${API_BASE_URL}/api/v1`. All endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>`.

### Admin endpoints (role: admin / superadmin)

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `POST` | `/notifications/send` | Send immediately OR schedule with `scheduledAt` |
| `GET` | `/notifications?page&limit&status&audience` | Paginated history |
| `GET` | `/notifications/:id` | Single record |
| `POST` | `/notifications/:id/cancel` | Cancel a `SCHEDULED` row before send |

### Send body

```json
{
  "title": "Festival reminder",
  "body": "Ganesh Chaturthi pooja begins at 6 AM tomorrow.",
  "audience": "ALL",
  "userIds": [],
  "data": { "deepLink": "/festivals/ganesh-chaturthi" },
  "imageUrl": "https://...",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-05-15T06:00:00.000Z"
}
```

- `title` required (max 120). `body` required (max 1000).
- `audience` ∈ `ALL | USERS | ADMINS | SUPERADMIN | USER_IDS` (default `ALL`). `userIds` required when `USER_IDS`.
- `data` values are coerced to strings (FCM data-payload rule).
- `scheduledAt` optional ISO future timestamp. Omit to send now.

### Send response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Notification queued for delivery",
  "data": {
    "notification": {
      "_id": "...",
      "title": "...",
      "body": "...",
      "audience": "ALL",
      "status": "PENDING" /* or SCHEDULED */,
      "scheduledAt": null,
      "sentAt": null,
      "successCount": 0,
      "failureCount": 0,
      "createdAt": "..."
    }
  }
}
```

### Notification payload the device receives

```
notification.title    = <title>
notification.body     = <body>
notification.imageUrl = <optional>
data.type             = "ADMIN_BROADCAST"
data.notificationId   = <mongo id>
data.<custom>         = <string>   // any keys passed in `data` from admin
```

Other backend pushes use the same envelope with different `type` values:

| `type` | Source | Suggested tap behavior |
|--------|--------|------------------------|
| `ADMIN_BROADCAST` | Admin broadcast | Open notifications inbox; optionally a detail screen |
| `ORDER_PLACED` | Order paid | Open Orders / order detail |
| `DONATION_RECEIVED` | Donation paid | Open `/donations/contributions` |

### Curl examples (for admin testing)

```bash
BASE_URL="https://satya-server-app-2.onrender.com/api/v1"
TOKEN="<ADMIN_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN>"

# Send to all users immediately
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/notifications/send" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Welcome","body":"Hello everyone"}'

# Send to regular users only
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/notifications/send" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Daily wisdom","body":"A new sloka awaits.","audience":"USERS"}'

# Schedule for later
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/notifications/send" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Tomorrow","body":"Pooja at 6 AM","scheduledAt":"2026-05-15T00:30:00.000Z"}'

# List history
curl "$BASE_URL/notifications?page=1&limit=20&status=SENT" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"

# Cancel a scheduled one
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/notifications/<id>/cancel" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

---

## Cursor prompt (paste into the Flutter repo)

Implement **Notifications support** in this Flutter app, on top of the existing FCM bootstrap (token registration is already wired via `POST /api/v1/fcm/register` — see `Flutter-fcm.plan`).

This adds three things:

1. **Receive + route** admin broadcast pushes (`data.type === "ADMIN_BROADCAST"`).
2. **Notifications Inbox** screen that mirrors the broadcast history a user has received.
3. **Admin "Send Push Notification" screen** for users with `role: admin | superadmin`, replicating the layout in the admin panel (Title, Message, Target Audience, Schedule).

### Stack (adapt to existing repo)

- Existing **Dio** client + auth interceptor — do not duplicate.
- Existing state library (Riverpod / Bloc / Provider) — do not introduce a second one.
- Existing router (GoRouter / Navigator) — do not switch.
- `firebase_messaging`, `flutter_local_notifications` (already present from FCM step).
- `intl` for formatting dates and counts.

### Backend endpoints to call (locked, do NOT change server)

User side:
- *(none new)* — pushes arrive via FCM; token registration already exists.

Admin side:
- `POST /api/v1/notifications/send` — body matches the table above.
- `GET /api/v1/notifications?page&limit&status&audience` — paginated history.
- `GET /api/v1/notifications/:id` — single record.
- `POST /api/v1/notifications/:id/cancel` — cancel scheduled.

### Models (`lib/features/notifications/data/models/`)

- `AppNotification`
  ```dart
  final String id;
  final String title;
  final String body;
  final String audience;       // ALL | USERS | ADMINS | SUPERADMIN | USER_IDS
  final String status;         // PENDING | SCHEDULED | SENDING | SENT | FAILED | CANCELLED
  final DateTime? scheduledAt;
  final DateTime? sentAt;
  final int successCount;
  final int failureCount;
  final DateTime createdAt;
  final String? imageUrl;
  final Map<String, dynamic>? data;
  ```
- `SendNotificationRequest` — exactly the body shape above; serializer must:
  - drop `userIds` if empty,
  - drop `scheduledAt` if null,
  - coerce all `data` values to `String` (FCM requirement).

### Repository (`lib/features/notifications/data/notifications_repository.dart`)

```dart
Future<({List<AppNotification> items, int total, int totalPages})> listNotifications({
  int page = 1, int limit = 10, String? status, String? audience,
});

Future<AppNotification> sendNotification(SendNotificationRequest req);

Future<AppNotification> getNotification(String id);

Future<AppNotification> cancelNotification(String id);
```

Map Dio errors to a typed `NotificationsException` exposing `status` + `message` from `response.data['message']`.

### Local inbox cache

The backend does NOT store per-user delivery rows, so the **inbox** is built from RemoteMessages cached locally:

- Add a tiny `notifications_inbox.dart` using `hive` (or `shared_preferences` with a JSON array) — only the last ~100 entries.
- Each entry: `{ id, title, body, data, receivedAt, read }`.
- Populated from every `onMessage` / background handler / `onMessageOpenedApp` / `getInitialMessage()`. Dedupe by `data.notificationId` when present.

This is the source of truth for the in-app **Notifications Inbox** screen.

### FCM routing

Extend the existing FCM message router to handle `data.type`:

```dart
switch (data['type']) {
  case 'ADMIN_BROADCAST':
    NotificationsInboxCache.add(message);
    router.go('/notifications');             // when tapped
    break;
  case 'ORDER_PLACED':
    router.go('/orders');
    break;
  case 'DONATION_RECEIVED':
    router.go('/donations/contributions');
    break;
  default:
    router.go('/notifications');
}
```

- `onMessage` (foreground): cache + show local notification banner; do NOT navigate.
- `onMessageOpenedApp` and `getInitialMessage()`: cache + navigate per `type`.
- Background isolate handler: cache + return; navigation happens later when the app opens.

### Screens (user side)

`lib/features/notifications/presentation/`

1. **NotificationsInboxScreen** (`/notifications`)
   - Lists cached pushes received on this device (newest first).
   - Each tile: title, body (truncated), relative time (`intl`), unread dot.
   - Tap a tile → mark read + show `NotificationDetailSheet` (full body + image if any).
   - Empty state: "No notifications yet."
   - Long-press → delete from local cache (does not affect the server).
   - Top app-bar action: **Mark all read**.

2. **NotificationDetailSheet** (modal bottom sheet)
   - Title, full body, image (if `imageUrl`), received time.
   - If `data.deepLink` present, render a primary CTA button that navigates to that route.

3. Bottom-nav / drawer entry: **Notifications** with an unread badge from cached state.

### Screens (admin side)

Render the next screen ONLY when `currentUser.role` is `admin` or `superadmin`.

4. **AdminSendNotificationScreen** (`/admin/notifications/send`)
   - Form matching the admin panel layout (see the reference image):
     - `Title` (required, max 120 chars, counter).
     - `Message` (required, max 1000 chars, multiline, counter).
     - `Target Audience` — dropdown: All Users (`ALL`), Users (`USERS`), Admins (`ADMINS`), Super Admin (`SUPERADMIN`). Skip `USER_IDS` from the UI for v1.
     - `Schedule (optional)` — date+time picker. Empty → send now. Validate future-only.
   - Submit button **Send Notification** with progress.
   - On success → snackbar "Notification queued" (or "Scheduled for <localized time>") and reset form.
   - On error → inline message from `NotificationsException`.

5. **AdminNotificationsHistoryScreen** (`/admin/notifications`)
   - Paginated list using `GET /notifications`.
   - Filter chips: ALL / SENT / SCHEDULED / FAILED / CANCELLED.
   - Per row: title, audience badge, status badge, success/total token counts, timestamp.
   - Tap → `AdminNotificationDetailScreen` showing full record.
   - If row is `SCHEDULED`: provide a **Cancel** action that calls `POST /notifications/:id/cancel`.

### Providers (Riverpod-style; adapt as needed)

- `notificationsRepositoryProvider`
- `inboxCacheProvider` — `StateNotifier` wrapping the local cache + unread count.
- `adminNotificationsListProvider` — `FutureProvider.family<…, NotificationsQuery>` paginated.
- `sendNotificationControllerProvider` — `AsyncNotifier` exposing `send(SendNotificationRequest req)`.
- `cancelNotificationControllerProvider` — `AsyncNotifier` exposing `cancel(String id)`.

### Routing

- `/notifications` → `NotificationsInboxScreen`
- `/admin/notifications` → `AdminNotificationsHistoryScreen`  (guard by role)
- `/admin/notifications/send` → `AdminSendNotificationScreen` (guard by role)

Add a top-level **Notifications** entry to the user drawer / bottom nav with the unread badge from `inboxCacheProvider`.

Add an **Admin → Send Push Notification** entry to the admin drawer (visible only for admins).

### Permissions and visibility

- Re-use the same iOS / Android 13+ permission prompts from the FCM step.
- For foreground notifications, render via `flutter_local_notifications`. Use a single channel `satya_default` already used by the rest of the app (do not create a new one per type).
- If the user has notifications disabled, the inbox still works (pushes received while online are still cached when the app handles `RemoteMessage`, but most apps won't see them in the tray).

### Validation rules to mirror the server

- `title`: required, 1–120 characters.
- `body`: required, 1–1000 characters.
- `audience`: one of `ALL | USERS | ADMINS | SUPERADMIN | USER_IDS`.
- `scheduledAt` if provided: must be strictly in the future.
- All `data` map values are converted to `String` before send.

### Do NOT

- Do not duplicate base URL or auth interceptor.
- Do not navigate from `onMessage` (foreground) — only from tap handlers.
- Do not call Firebase Admin SDK from Flutter.
- Do not store the entire history server-side per user — the inbox is a **device-local cache**.
- Do not edit any backend files.

### Acceptance criteria

1. User receives a push from `POST /notifications/send` while app is **background** → tray notification visible.
2. Tap → app opens to **Notifications Inbox** (default) or the deep link if `data.deepLink` is present.
3. Inbox shows the new notification at the top, unread badge updates, mark-all-read clears the badge.
4. Foreground push → cache updates + local in-app heads-up notification appears.
5. Admin logs in, opens **Send Push Notification**, fills Title + Message, picks `All Users`, hits Send → success snackbar; another logged-in test device receives the push.
6. Admin schedules for ~2 minutes in future → row appears in `AdminNotificationsHistoryScreen` as `SCHEDULED`. After the scheduled time the row flips to `SENT` and the user device gets the push.
7. Admin opens a `SCHEDULED` row and taps **Cancel** → row becomes `CANCELLED` and is NOT delivered.
8. `flutter analyze` clean; light + dark theme both render correctly.

### Final step

Run `flutter analyze` and `dart format .`. Provide a short "How to test" checklist mirroring the acceptance criteria above.

---

End of Cursor prompt.

## Quick manual QA checklist (after deploy)

1. Open admin panel form (Title / Message / Target Audience / Schedule).
2. Send to `All Users` → confirm at least one test device receives the push.
3. Open the Flutter app → tap the notification → inbox screen shows it at the top.
4. Schedule a notification 2 minutes in the future → device receives it on time.
5. Schedule another, then `Cancel` before its time → device does NOT receive it.
